sol:'A static field has zero curl, so its line integral around any loop vanishes and endpoint differences are path-blind — that is what makes $V$ well-defined in the first place. (Time-varying $B$ breaks the spell via Faraday: the curl becomes $-\\partial_t\\vec{B}$.)',
