sol:'Integrate ring strips: $E = \\frac{\\sigma}{2\\varepsilon_0}\\int_0^{R}\\frac{x\\,r\'\\,dr\'}{(x^{2}+r\'^{2})^{3/2}} = \\frac{\\sigma}{2\\varepsilon_0}\\left[1 - \\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x^{2}+R^{2}}}\\right]$. The two limits are the lesson: $R \\to \\infty$ gives the sheet $\\sigma/(2\\varepsilon_0)$, and $x \\gg R$ collapses to a point charge.',
